"video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "cover.png", "id": "1077288725353822", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/593867383_1077288732020488_4158929673329885414_n.png?_nc_cat=101&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=LQclCKfaUawQ7kNvwGocBCX&_nc_oc=AdoVFo1uZVgB2oE7uOH-VX9B3-8Sqy5aZbzejAcpl1P0-2vMJE461DCmUkzRp91gBjo&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQQCbxflX4jVZcngC1dL64fv3f9JlOckLpkfIulndWIXTQ&oe=6AF714E5"}, "display_name": "Sky Unveiled", "keywords": ["planetarium", "stargazing", "astronomy", "constellations", "stars"], "long_description": "Most of us live under skies washed out by city lights. Sky Unveiled gives you back the night.\n\nPick your city from over 34,000 and any date and time. You stand in a quiet meadow, a tent behind you, under the sky as it really is from that place: the Milky Way, the Moon in its true phase, all seven planets and the 9,000 or so stars your eyes could see on a truly dark night. Watch the sun set, then turn the light pollution down to pristine and see what the city has been hiding.\n\nYour own star-party host\nPoint at a star and pull the trigger, and a voice tells you about it, like the guide with the laser pointer at a star party: what it is, how to find it and, now and then, an old Greek or Arabic story. There are 375 of these, for every named star, all 88 constellations, every marked sight, the Moon and each planet, with captions. On your first night, the host shows you round.\n\nA closer look\nOpen a star, planet or deep-sky sight in binoculars or a telescope: clusters break into stars, Saturn shows its rings, and many have a long-exposure photograph to compare.\n\nThe sky starts clean. Add only what you want:\n- Lines and names for all 88 constellations\n- Markers for 194 sights: the 110 Messier galaxies, nebulae and clusters, 52 more, and double and carbon stars\n- Altitude-azimuth and equatorial grids\n- Time-lapse, to watch the whole sky wheel overhead\n\nAt night, crickets, wind and a distant owl; at dawn, birdsong. Play standing, or sit back and turn the sky with the thumbstick.", "short_description": "Your sky. Without the city lights.\n\nStand in a quiet meadow under the real sky above your own city, on any night you choose, and lift the light pollution to watch the Milky Way appear. Point at a star, planet or constellation and your own star-party host tells you what it is, how to find it and, now and then, the old stories told about it. Look closer through binoculars or a telescope, or speed up time to watch the whole sky wheel overhead."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://sky.meridianfield.online/privacy/", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Meridian Field", "support_website_url": "https://sky.meridianfield.online/about/", "website_url": "https://sky.meridianfield.online/about/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_SOME", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1043107547362485"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "REQUIRED", "play_area": "NO_MOVEMENT", "recommended_graphics": null, "recommended_memory_gb": null, "recommended_processor": null, "supported_in_app_languages": ["en"], "supported_input_devices": ["OCULUS_TOUCH"], "supported_player_modes": ["SITTING", "STANDING"], "supported_tracking_modes": [], "user_interaction_modes": ["SINGLE_USER"], "id": "1309069085633711"}, "review_messages": []}]}, "cover_square_image": {"uri": "https://scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/499624619_1114641264893742_6625170586148019860_n.png?stp=dst-png_s360x360&_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=o1YqwBLagU4Q7kNvwFGgFB_&_nc_oc=Adp20UlZOp3nRrD1D7eBR4z85q2ze4kK8wKu-pY5gplWbaLPWTnH0cpfUIRAAhKdpTs&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQTur3g2kdkJnmOve29BjRrI